<Rive version="1" kind="fragment">
    <!--
      WatchToss: "Keep it. Seriously." We throw the watch away, then, just kidding, bring it back.
      The six "Pose N ..." animations are single-frame holds keying every animated property:
      Idle plays Pose 1, End plays Pose 6, and the Toss timeline (330 frames at 60 fps, 5.5 s)
      runs from the one to the other through the other four.
        0.00-0.60  hold, a small bob          1.35-2.40  empty beat; `joke` fires at 1.70 s (frame 102)
        0.60-1.10  wind-up, squash            2.40-3.20  boomerang return, caught at 3.10
        1.10-1.35  throw, release at 1.20     3.20-4.10  set down, screen on at 3.40, two pats
                                              4.10-5.50  blips to the phone, logo on, thumbs-up

      800 x 600, no artboard fill (the page's dark card shows through). Draw order, front first:
      pat marks, blips, blip trail, whoosh, return arc, hand, watch, floor shadow, phone.
      The watch sits BEHIND the hand in every pose: the fist grips its strap, the catch and the
      pat draw the hand over it.

      Hand: origin at the wrist, fingers up (-y). Fingers and thumb are drawn behind the palm;
      each digit keys rotation, capsule height, tip y and nail opacity (tip = -length).
      scaleX -1 turns the back of the hand into the palm (nails off, palm lines on).
      Watch: origin at the face centre; Screen On opacity is the screen. When held, its centre
      is (0, -222) in hand space, rotated with the hand.

      View model WatchToss (auto-bound default instance):
        play (trigger, in)   starts the toss from the Idle pose
        skip (trigger, in)   from any state, goes to the End pose (the payoff)
        joke (trigger, out)  fired by the timeline when "Just kidding." should appear
    -->
